  "Content": {
    "Html": "<p><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/book/how-to-survive-a-pandemic/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><em>How to Survive a Pandemic</em></a> is now out! Note: if you checked on Amazon and noticed the Kindle and paperback versions were not available before, <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Survive-Pandemic-Michael-FACLM-Greger-ebook/dp/B086S3XKBC/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-cke-saved-href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Survive-Pandemic-Michael-FACLM-Greger-ebook/dp/B086S3XKBC/\">they are now</a>! Join my <a href=\"https://NutritionFacts.org/subscribe/\">email list</a> to receive the preface of the book for free. </p>\n<p>I have a feeling many think <em><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/books/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">How Not to Die</a></em> is my first book, but it’s actually my 4th. Before I started NutritionFacts.org and switched to working on chronic disease, I had a career as Public Health Director at HSUS in Washington, DC specializing in emerging infectious disease. It was in that role that I was invited to defend Oprah, appeared on the Colbert Report, lectured at NIH and the Conference on World Affairs, and got to testify before Congress.</p>\n<p>With my <em><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/book/how-not-to-diet/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">How Not to Diet</a></em> book tour suspended, the COVID-19 crisis allowed me an opportunity to draw on my past expertise to fast-track this new book. </p>\n<p>If you haven’t seen it yet, we’ve put up a resource page all about COVID-19 with videos, links to my pandemic blog post and special Q&amp;A sessions, a DIY hand sanitizer recipe, and more. Check it out <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/covid-19/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">here</a>. And I’ve been doing a bunch of interviews lately, notably one with Moby and Joaquin Phoenix that you can watch <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GxdUwh98gmo\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-cke-saved-href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GxdUwh98gmo\">here</a>, as well as an article from <a href=\"https://www.vox.com/future-perfect/2020/4/22/21228158/coronavirus-pandemic-risk-factory-farming-meat\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-cke-saved-href=\"https://www.vox.com/future-perfect/2020/4/22/21228158/coronavirus-pandemic-risk-factory-farming-meat\">Vox</a>. </p>\n<h4 class=\"null\"><strong>New webinar – June 26</strong></h4>\n<p><a href=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/05/B12_recommendation_webinar_promotional_IG.png/\"><img decoding=\"async\" class=\" wp-image-63698 alignleft\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/05/B12_recommendation_webinar_promotional_IG-1024x991.png\" alt=\"B12_recommendation_webinar_promotional_IG\" width=\"200\" height=\"193\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/05/B12_recommendation_webinar_promotional_IG-1024x991.png 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/05/B12_recommendation_webinar_promotional_IG-960x930.png 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/05/B12_recommendation_webinar_promotional_IG-768x744.png 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/05/B12_recommendation_webinar_promotional_IG-720x697.png 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/05/B12_recommendation_webinar_promotional_IG-540x523.png 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/05/B12_recommendation_webinar_promotional_IG.png 1134w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 200px) 100vw, 200px\"/></a>On June 26th I’m going to be doing a 1.5-hour live <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/webinar/latest-b12-recommendation/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">webinar</a> to explain the rationale for my new vitamin B12 recommendations and answer any questions you may have. I’ll start out with a discussion of the symptoms of B12 deficiency and then explain how I arrived at what I consider the optimal dose of vitamin B12 supplements in children, adults, the elderly, and during pregnancy. I’ll clarify why cyanocobalamin (<em>not</em> methylcobalamin) is the best type of vitamin B12 supplement and address the data suggesting B12 supplements cause acne, bone fractures, and lung cancer. I’ll also cover the healthiest food sources of B12 for those that don’t want to take supplements. I hope you’ll join me!</p>\n<p>Register by making a donation of any amount through <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.z2systems.com/np/clients/nutritionfacts/donation.jsp?campaign=49&amp;&amp;test=true\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-cke-saved-href=\"https://nutritionfacts.z2systems.com/np/clients/nutritionfacts/donation.jsp?campaign=49&amp;&amp;test=true\">this form</a>.</p>\n<p><strong>Registration ends:</strong> June 19<br/>\n<strong>Webinar date &amp; time: </strong>June 26, 2:00-3:30pm ET</p>\n<p> </p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><a href=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month.png/\"><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignnone size-large wp-image-60211\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month-1024x331.png\" alt=\"Top 3 Videos of the Month\" width=\"460\" height=\"149\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month-1024x331.png 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month-960x310.png 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month-768x248.png 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month-720x233.png 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month-540x174.png 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2019/08/Top-3-Videos-of-the-Month.png 1108w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 460px) 100vw, 460px\"/></a> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p><a href=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/05/Corona-Q-A-Wide.png/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"wp-image-63700 alignleft\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/05/Corona-Q-A-Wide-1024x536.png\" alt=\"COVID Q&amp;A Thumbnail\" width=\"201\" height=\"105\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/05/Corona-Q-A-Wide-1024x536.png 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/05/Corona-Q-A-Wide-960x502.png 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/05/Corona-Q-A-Wide-768x402.png 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/05/Corona-Q-A-Wide.png 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/05/Corona-Q-A-Wide-720x377.png 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/05/Corona-Q-A-Wide-540x283.png 540w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 201px) 100vw, 201px\"/></a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kMsHN2BdOzs\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-cke-saved-href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kMsHN2BdOzs\">COVID-19 Live Q&amp;A</a></p>\n<p>Replay of my COVID-19 Q&amp;A last month.</p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p><a href=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/05/50-12.jpg/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"wp-image-63008 alignleft\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/05/50-12-1024x576.jpg\" alt=\"Benefits of Quinoa for Lowering Triglycerides\" width=\"201\" height=\"113\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/05/50-12-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/05/50-12-960x540.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/05/50-12-768x432.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/05/50-12-480x270.jpg 480w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/05/50-12-1200x675.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/05/50-12-720x405.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/05/50-12-540x304.jpg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/05/50-12.jpg 1920w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 201px) 100vw, 201px\"/></a><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/benefits-of-quinoa-for-lowering-triglycerides/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Benefits of Quinoa for Lowering Triglycerides</a></p>\n<p>How does the nutrition and health benefits of quinoa compare to whole grains, and does it aid in lowering triglycerides?</p>\n<p> </p>\n<p><a href=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/04/50-5.jpg/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"wp-image-62791 alignleft\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/04/50-5-1024x576.jpg\" alt=\"The Role of Processed Foods in the Obesity Epidemic\" width=\"201\" height=\"113\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/04/50-5-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/04/50-5-960x540.jpg 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/04/50-5-768x432.jpg 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/04/50-5-480x270.jpg 480w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/04/50-5-1200x675.jpg 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/04/50-5-720x405.jpg 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/04/50-5-540x304.jpg 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2020/04/50-5.jpg 1920w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 201px) 100vw, 201px\"/></a><a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/the-role-of-processed-foods-in-the-obesity-epidemic/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">The Role of Processed Foods in the Obesity Epidemic</a></p>\n<p>The rise in the U.S. calorie supply responsible for national weight gain and the obesity epidemic wasn’t just about more food, but a different kind of food – processed food.</p>\n<p> </p>\n<h4 class=\"null\"><strong>Live Q&amp;As May 28</strong></h4>\n<p><a href=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/05/LiveQANewsletter-Square.png/\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\" wp-image-53879 alignleft\" src=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/05/LiveQANewsletter-Square-1024x1024.png\" alt=\"Live Q&amp;A\" width=\"198\" height=\"198\" srcset=\"https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/05/LiveQANewsletter-Square-1024x1024.png 1024w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/05/LiveQANewsletter-Square-960x960.png 960w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/05/LiveQANewsletter-Square-768x768.png 768w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/05/LiveQANewsletter-Square-500x500.png 500w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/05/LiveQANewsletter-Square-1200x1200.png 1200w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/05/LiveQANewsletter-Square-720x720.png 720w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/05/LiveQANewsletter-Square-540x540.png 540w, https://assets.nutritionfacts.org/2018/05/LiveQANewsletter-Square.png 2000w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 198px) 100vw, 198px\"/></a>Every month now I do Q&amp;As live from my treadmill, and <em><strong>Thursday, May 28</strong></em> is the day.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Facebook Live</strong>: At 12:00 p.m. ET go to our <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/NutritionFacts.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-cke-saved-href=\"https://www.facebook.com/NutritionFacts.org/\">Facebook page</a> to watch live and ask questions.</li>\n<li><strong>YouTube Live Stream: </strong>At 1:00 p.m. ET go <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/c/NutritionfactsOrgMD/live\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" data-cke-saved-href=\"https://www.youtube.com/c/NutritionfactsOrgMD/live\">here</a> to watch live and ask even more questions! </li>\n</ul>\n<p>You can now find links to all of my past live Q&amp;As right <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/live/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">here</a> on NutritionFacts.org. If that’s not enough, remember I have an audio podcast to keep you company at <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/audio/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">https://nutritionfacts.org/audio.</a></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p>In health,<br/>\n<b>Michael Greger, M.D.</b></p>\n<p>PS: If you haven’t yet, you can subscribe to my free videos <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/subscribe/\"><b>here</b></a><b> </b>and watch my live, year-in-review presentations:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>2019: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/evidence-based-weight-loss-live-presentation/\"><b>Evidence-Based Weight Loss</b></a></li>\n<li>2016: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/how-not-to-die/\"><u><b>How Not To Die: The Role of Diet in Preventing, Arresting, and Reversing Our Top 15 Killers</b></u></a></li>\n<li>2015: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/food-as-medicine/\"><u><b>Food as Medicine: Preventing and Treating the Most Dreaded Diseases with Diet</b></u></a></li>\n<li>2014: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/from-table-to-able/\"><u><b>From Table to Able: Combating Disabling Diseases with Food</b></u></a></li>\n<li>2013: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/more-than-an-apple-a-day-preventing-our-most-common-diseases/\"><u><b>More Than an Apple a Day</b></u></a></li>\n<li>2012: <a href=\"https://nutritionfacts.org/video/uprooting-the-leading-causes-of-death/\"><u><b>Uprooting the Leading Causes of Death</b></u></a></li>\n</ul>"
